--TEST--
`streamAs<T>` over a class carrying no `#[Db\Derive]` is refused while compiling, on both spellings of the member — `rule:core-classes/derive-attribute`, `rule:core-classes/db-streaming`, spec § 18
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:core-classes/derive-attribute` makes hydration opt-in, so a class with
// no `#[Db\Derive]` is perfectly well formed and stays so: it is only a call
// that asks a row to *become* one that has no column mapping to work from. That
// question is the whole program's — the class is routinely declared in a file
// the walk has not reached — so it is answered after the walk rather than where
// the call is written, which is what `nvs_types::derive`'s `check_row_sites`
// exists for.
//
// The same refusal `queryAs<T>` takes, said of the member that never holds a
// result set: what a walk cannot build it cannot build one row at a time
// either.
use Core\Db\Transaction;

class Plain {
    public uint $id;

    public function constructor(uint $id)
    {
        $this->id = $id;
    }
}

class People {
    public static function walking(Transaction $tx): Core\Db\Stream<Plain>
    {
        return $tx->streamAs<Plain>("select id from people", []);
    }
}

var $db = Core\Db::connect("main");
var $walk = $db->streamAs<Plain>("select id from people", []);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0806]: `Plain` carries no `#[Db\Derive]`, so `Core\Db\Transaction::streamAs` has no mapping
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
